! =============================================================================
! SaltFoss Training — Segment 2 (0:08-0:16): First FLiBe equilibrium
! =============================================================================
! Teaching point: input is ELEMENTS, not compounds. We give Li, Be, F — the
! code decides what forms. Composition is nominally 2LiF + 1BeF2 (the eutectic
! stoichiometry), with F perturbed by 1 part in 400,000 to avoid the exact
! under-determined case covered in Segment 3.
!
! Run:   ./bin/InputScriptMode inputs/training/saltfoss/01_flibe_basic.ti
! Expect: single MSFL (SUBQ) liquid phase, trace gas_ideal, DEBUG: Successful exit.
! Walk the printed blocks: phase assemblage -> speciation -> element chemical
! potentials -> integral Gibbs energy -> functional norm (convergence measure).
! =============================================================================
temperature       = 900
pressure          = 1.0
mass(3)           = 2.0        ! Li
mass(4)           = 1.0        ! Be
mass(9)           = 4.00001    ! F  (2*LiF + 1*BeF2, perturbed)
temperature unit  = K
pressure unit     = atm
mass unit         = moles
data file         = data/MSD-TC_V4.1_Fluorides_No_Func.dat
print mode        = 2
